    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2192" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ambŭlātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		ambulo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one that walks about</i>, i.e., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An idler</i>, <i>lounger</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vilicus ne sit ambulator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 5, 2</span></i>
			 (cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5, 2</span></i>: minus
			licebit ambulare); <i><span class="en">Col. 1, 8, 7</span></i>.—*
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A pedlar</i>, <i>hawker</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Transtiberinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					1, 42</span></i>
			 (not found elsewhere).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
